# US-0072 (EPIC-0003 voice A1c): the TLS proxy of deploy/compose/voice.yml (profile `lan`). One hostname and one owner-supplied
# certificate, two sites: the web app on VOICE_HTTPS_PORT and LiveKit signalling on VOICE_LIVEKIT_TLS_PORT.
#
# - No access log (no `log` directive in a site): the LiveKit token travels in the signalling URL's query, so an access log would
#   record it. Caddy's DEFAULT logger still writes handler errors (http.log.error, with a `request` object whose `uri` holds the
#   query; Cookie and Authorization are redacted there, the query is not): during a LiveKit outage every reconnect to
#   /rtc?access_token=<JWT> is a 502. So the global `log default` below deletes the parameters livekit-client 2.23.0 puts in the
#   signalling URL that carry the token or the participant's join data (access_token, join_request, sid) from every logged request
#   URI, and logs at ERROR only (no INFO entries at all). UNVERIFIED until the owner run of Task 15, which must check that the Caddy
#   container log holds no token during a forced 502 (LiveKit stopped while a participant reconnects).
# - No trusted_proxies and no header directive for X-Forwarded-For: Caddy then REPLACES that header with the client's own address,
#   which the web app's throttles rely on (docs/THREAT_MODEL.md, "Client address, TRUST_PROXY and the per-role throttles").
# - The LiveKit site forwards only /rtc* (signalling and validation) and drops the Cookie header: the __Host-scenecoach cookie is sent
#   to every port of the host, and LiveKit's HTTP port also serves its server API. Everything else answers 404.
# - admin off (no admin endpoint); HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 only (UDP is not published, so no HTTP/3); no port 80 redirect server.
{
	admin off
	auto_https disable_redirects
	servers {
		protocols h1 h2
	}
	log default {
		output stderr
		format filter {
			wrap json
			fields {
				request>uri query {
					delete access_token
					delete join_request
					delete sid
				}
			}
		}
		level ERROR
	}
}

{$VOICE_HOSTNAME}:{$VOICE_HTTPS_PORT} {
	tls /certs/cert.pem /certs/key.pem
	reverse_proxy {$VOICE_WEB_UPSTREAM}
}

{$VOICE_HOSTNAME}:{$VOICE_LIVEKIT_TLS_PORT} {
	tls /certs/cert.pem /certs/key.pem
	handle /rtc* {
		reverse_proxy livekit:7880 {
			header_up -Cookie
		}
	}
	handle {
		respond 404
	}
}
